'''Thyon''' ([[IPA]]: ), officially the '''Empire of Thyon''', is a country in the continent of [[???]] on the planet [[Basis]]. It borders [[COUNTRY]] to the north, [[COUNTRY]] to the east, and [[COUNTRY]] to the south. Thyon is a federated monarchy, which consists of three constituent kingdoms ([[Thyon (constituent kingdom)|Thyon]], [[Merin]] and the [[Maritime Union]] (which itself consists of three states), and four imperially administered [[Provinces of Thyon|provinces]] ([[Aunan]], [[Luser]], [[SOUTH]] and [[SOUTHWEST]]. Each constituent kingdom has a monarch, along with an elected government. The capital city is [[Polamdi]], and the largest city is [[Rhempo]], closely followed by the cultural and historical capitals of [[Fepo]] and [[Khapo]]. 

In the [[Age]], from 3000 BCE, the territory of present-day Thyon was inhabited by early [[Auser civilisation]]s, centred on the central [[Auser River]] plains. The agriculturally focused Auser civilisation and culture spread from the central plains toward the [[OCEAN]] coast and up river to the Auser Uplands. The [[Cunerians]], a coastal Auser tribe, gradually expanded their territory until founding the [[Cunerian Empire]] in 1000 BCE. The Cunerian Empire expanded Old Thyonese language and culture across southern [[continent]]. Following the [[Northern Invasion]] in 990 CE, the empire collapsed and was divided into various duchies. Following the [[Battle of Volapo]] in 1011, the [[Duchy of Merin]] was incorporated into the [[NORTHERNER Empire]], with Thyo-Merinese culture divided and subdued in Merin. After 200 years of Northerner rule, the events of [[Thyo-Merinese Rejuvenation]] led to the establishment of the [[Kingdom of Merin]] in 1445 CE, the expulsion of Northerner influence, and the establishment of the [[Kingdom of Thyon]] in 1623 CE. The [[Rejuvenation Era]], saw Merin and Thyon fight battles for influence over the Thyo-Merinese world. 

Formation of the unified Thyon nation-state began in 2060 CE, led by the [[Kindgom of Thyon]], and established the Thyonese Empire in 2100 CE. The newly established empire expanded to conquer the Auser Uplands region of Central [[continent]], as well [[Lower Thyonese language|Lower Thyonese]] speaking regions in [[Southern Continent]]. 

Thyon is a member of the [[Basis Forum]]. It is also a member of the [[International Trade Federation]] and the [[Basis Climatic Organization]], and hosts the headquarters of several international organizations, including the [[Basis Development Bank]]. Thyon is a developed country with one of the largest economies on Basis.

