==Government and politics==
Thyon is a federal constitutional elective monarchy, made up of three constituent kingdoms and four imperially-administered provinces. The constituent kingdoms of Thyon and Merin have their own hereditary monarchs, while the Maritime Union has a rotating Council of Presidents. The imperial monarch is known as the Archon. 

Thyon has a federal or imperial parliament, known as the [[Federal Assembly of Thyon|Federal Assembly]], which is the responsible legislature for powers reserved for the federal government. The Archon appoints a Federal Cabinet appointed from members of the federal parliament, which in practice is always the party which commands a majority in the Federal Assembly.
{{Main|Politics of Thyon}}
===Monarchy and royal family===
{{Main|Monarchy of Thyon}}
Thyon is a constitutional monarchy, nominally elected, but in practice the elected Archon has been the hereditary King of Thyon since 2170 CE. The [[House of Ga]] has controlled the monarchy since 1970.

The [[Acts of Constitution]] define the relationship of between the Archon, the government and the Federal Assembly. 

