===Law===
Thyon has no official written constitution, but the [[Treaty of Gergumlaauser]], the [[Acts of Constitution (Thyon)|Acts of Constitution]], and the [[Acts of the Judiciary]] form the constitutional framework of Thyon. The Treaty of Gergumlaauser defines the powers of the Federal Assembly and the constituent kingdoms, modified by the Acts of Constitution. The Federal Assembly and constituent Parliaments are restricted from making laws which contravene the Treaty or the Acts of Constitution. The Treaty and later the Acts of Constitution established a process by which the constitutional framework can be amended. This requires a supermajority in all Parliaments of the constituent kingdoms and the Federal Assembly, before obtaining royal assent via a special session of the Federal Council. 

The Federal Assembly may only pass laws on specific matters permitted by the constitutional framework, or if a matter is referred by the a constituent kingdom's parliament. Likewise, constituent kingdoms cannot pass laws on matters reserved for the Federal Assembly. Imperial and constituent laws which contravene the constitutional framework can be referred to the [[Federal Court of Thyon|Federal Court]], the supreme court of last resort of Thyon, to be struck down.

There is a federal judiciary headed by the Federal Court, the supreme court, which has unlimited and final jurisdiction for all civil, constitutional and criminal matters. Each constituent kingdom has their own judiciary and legal system. An ability to appeal constituent cases to the Federal Court was established by the Acts of Judiciary in 2380 CE. The federal judiciary is organised into appeals, provincial and specialist courts. The Federal Appeals Court hears appeals on cases referred from the lower provincial and specialist courts. The provincial and specialist courts serve as courts of original jurisdiction for cases in the provinces or in areas of law which are the domain of the Federal Assembly. 

===Constituent kingdoms and provinces===
Thyon has three [[constituent kingdoms of Thyon|constituent kingdoms]] and four [[provinces of Thyon|provinces]], which are directly administered by the imperial government. Each constituent kingdom retains a monarch and a Parliament with the ability to pass laws on all matters except matters reserved to the Federal government. 

The [[Maritime Union]], while considered a constituent kingdom, is itself a union of smaller states. Prior to the Treaty of Gergumlaauser, the maritime trading principalities of [[Noeteo]], [[Gal]] and [[Melapo]] had formed a loose union to advance shared interests. There is no unified governmental organs aside from the [[Council of Presidents]], which consists of the [[President of Noeteo]], [[President of Melapo|Melapo]] and the [[Prince of Gal]], and the [[Supreme Court of the Maritime Union]]. The Council of Presidents is responsible for intergovernmental relations on behalf of the Maritime Union. Each Maritime state has its own executive government, legislature and judiciary. Two of the Maritime states are no longer monarchies, having adopted presidential systems. 

